DAY 9 - SET & DICTIONARY

SET
- Set is an unordered collection of unique elements.
- Duplicates are automatically removed.
- Created using { } or set().
- Useful for removing duplicates and mathematical set operations.

Creating Sets:
Empty Set:
s = set()

Example:
data = {10, 20, 30, 20, 10}
Output:
{10, 20, 30}

SET OPERATIONS

1. Membership
in
not in

2. Union
Combines all unique elements.
a | b

3. Intersection
Returns common elements.
a & b

4. Difference
Elements present in first set but not second.
a - b

5. Symmetric Difference
Elements present in either set but not both.
a ^ b

6. Subset
a <= b

7. Superset
a >= b


